In this technical dialogue, AI expert Chip Huyen emphasizes that practical user feedback and data preparation are far more critical to building successful applications than obsessively chasing the latest industry hype. She dismantles the common misconception that performance gains come from fine-tuning or picking the "best" model, arguing instead that the real value lies in robust evaluation (evals) and system thinking to address holistic product needs. The conversation explores the mechanics of Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), shifting the focus from model creation to the "post-training" phase where specific business utility is defined. Ultimately, Huyen suggests that we are facing an idea crisis where the abundance of powerful tools highlights a lack of creative vision, urging builders to focus on solving concrete frustrations rather than simply implementing complex technology for its own sake.